<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-2315] Local timestamps fields for Avro schema are not supported</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2315</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Avro schema supports the creation of local timestampe fields:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
LocalTimestampMillis datetimeType = LogicalTypes.localTimestampMillis();
field = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Schema.Field(attrDesc.getAttributeName(), Schema.createUnion(datetimeType.addToSchema(Schema.create(Schema.Type.LONG), Schema.create(Schema.Type.NULL)), doc, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But since there is no support in the AvroSchemaConverter.convertLogicalType method, these fields end up as BIGINT (as reported in e.g. Apache Drill).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
